/* ---- priority ------------------------------------------------------------
   How much it matters, which is a different axis from how far along it is.
   It lives in the header, where four numbers describe the shape of the day,
   and on the detail screen. It is deliberately absent from the list card: a
   red flag on every second row stops meaning anything, and the card's job is
   to say what has happened, not to re-argue the ranking. Only the top two
   carry colour — if Normal and Low were tinted too, nothing would stand out.
   -------------------------------------------------------------------------- */
/* Four levels, four colours, on the ladder the rest of the app already uses:
   crit → warn → info → ok, the same four the status pills are drawn from. It
   descends as heat — red, amber, blue, green — so the row is read as a
   temperature rather than four unrelated swatches, and Normal and Low are
   legible as *their own* levels instead of as "not the tinted ones". */
/* The words are the Wave Resident app's — High / Normal / Low — so a resident
   who set "High" and the supervisor reading the board are naming the same
   thing. The key stays `urgent` because the data and every predicate already
   speak it; only the label the supervisor reads has changed. */
const PRIO = {
