   Picking who goes to a flat is the supervisor's single most consequential
   act: it compares eight facts about a dozen people, and half of them were
   below the fold of a sheet that could only ever show two and a half cards.
   It gets a full screen, with the Wave Resident app's helper-card shape —
   photograph first, name and trade on one line, the small facts on their own
   tinted bar underneath — so a provider reads the same way here as a maid or
   a cook does over there.
